menu "feckless_umode"

    config FECKLESS_UMODE_PREEMPTIBLE
        bool "Let interrupts land inside a U-mode window (experimental)"
        default n
        help
            By default a window raises the CLIC threshold to its maximum, so
            no interrupt is taken while the boxed program runs; they are
            serviced at the next syscall or exit.  Enabling this leaves the
            threshold alone and re-pends edge-triggered lines claimed by the
            private vector.  On an ESP32-P4 rev 1.3 Tab5 (u-feckless-0016)
            this stopped the tick on CPU0 and tripped the interrupt watchdog;
            leave it off unless investigating that.

    config FECKLESS_UMODE_CALL_STATS
        bool "Log what a boxed app's host calls cost (diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            u-feckless-0029. Every CONFIG_FECKLESS_UMODE_CALL_STATS_SECONDS
            the loaded app's busiest host calls are logged: how many a
            second, the microseconds each took in the host, and the share
            of a second that is -- and, per thread, how many calls it made
            and how long it spent in them. A host call is a trap each way,
            so an app that makes tens of thousands a second (soft-float
            doubles are one each) shows here. Costs two timer reads and two
            atomic adds a call.

    config FECKLESS_UMODE_CALL_STATS_SECONDS
        int "Seconds between call-stat lines"
        depends on FECKLESS_UMODE_CALL_STATS
        default 5
        range 1 60

endmenu
